# Converting `std::string` to `std::vector` in C++

Depending on your goal, there are several common ways to convert a `std::string` to a `std::vector`. Below are the most typical scenarios with examples.

---

## 1. String to `std::vector<char>`

Convert each character in the string into a vector element.

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>

std::string str = "hello";
std::vector<char> vec(str.begin(), str.end());
```

---

## 2. String to `std::vector<std::string>` (Split by Delimiter)

Split a string into substrings based on a delimiter (e.g., comma, space).

### C++17 and Later (Using `std::string_view`)

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <string_view>

std::vector<std::string> split(const std::string& str, char delimiter) {
    std::vector<std::string> tokens;
    std::string_view sv(str);
    size_t start = 0, end = 0;

    while ((end = sv.find(delimiter, start)) != std::string_view::npos) {
        tokens.emplace_back(sv.substr(start, end - start));
        start = end + 1;
    }
    tokens.emplace_back(sv.substr(start));
    return tokens;
}
```

### Pre-C++17 Version

```cpp
#include <sstream>

std::vector<std::string> split(const std::string& str, char delimiter) {
    std::vector<std::string> tokens;
    std::stringstream ss(str);
    std::string token;

    while (std::getline(ss, token, delimiter)) {
        tokens.push_back(token);
    }
    return tokens;
}
```

**Example:**

```cpp
std::string input = "apple,banana,cherry";
std::vector<std::string> result = split(input, ',');
// result = {"apple", "banana", "cherry"}
```

---

## 3. String of Numbers to `std::vector<int>` or `std::vector<double>`

Parse numeric values from a string into a vector.

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <sstream>

std::vector<int> stringToIntVector(const std::string& str) {
    std::vector<int> result;
    std::stringstream ss(str);
    int value;

    while (ss >> value) {
        result.push_back(value);
    }
    return result;
}
```

**Example:**

```cpp
std::string input = "10 20 30 40";
std::vector<int> nums = stringToIntVector(input);
// nums = {10, 20, 30, 40}
```

---

## Summary Table

| Goal                             | Method                                  |
|----------------------------------|------------------------------------------|
| String → `vector<char>`          | Constructor with iterators               |
| String → `vector<string>`        | Split by delimiter (stringstream/view)   |
| String → `vector<int/double>`    | Parse with `stringstream`                |

---

